# Build It, Show It — Cursor Adapter

This repo is a **7-stage harness** that walks a student founder from a raw idea to
a clickable demo. The harness was built for Claude Code (slash commands in
`.claude/skills/`) but all stage logic lives in plain SKILL.md files that Cursor
can read and follow directly.

## How to run a stage in Cursor

There are no slash commands here. When the user says **"run stage N"**, **"do stage
N"**, or names a stage (e.g. "let's do the problem stage"):

1. Read `.claude/skills/<stage>/SKILL.md` — that file is the complete instruction set
2. Read `.claude/skills/shared/HARNESS.md` — shared conventions (run folder, artifact format, interview rules)
3. Follow the skill exactly: interview → do the work → save artifact

One Cursor-specific difference: the skills use `AskUserQuestion` (a Claude Code
tool). In Cursor, **ask questions as plain chat messages** instead — same questions,
same flow, just as conversation.

## Stage map

| User says | Read this skill | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| stage 1 / problem | `.claude/skills/1-problem/SKILL.md` | Name one user + one pain, create run folder |
| stage 2 / spec | `.claude/skills/2-spec/SKILL.md` | Cut to the smallest buildable screen |
| stage 3 / opportunity | `.claude/skills/3-opportunity/SKILL.md` | Competitors, demand signals, market size |
| stage 4a / lovable | `.claude/skills/4a-lovable/SKILL.md` | No-code route — 3–4 Lovable prompts |
| stage 4b / scope / design | `.claude/skills/4b-scope-design/SKILL.md` | Lock the screen + set the brand |
| stage 5 / build | `.claude/skills/5-build/SKILL.md` | Wire the screen into the starter template |
| stage 6 / test | `.claude/skills/6-test-iterate/SKILL.md` | Walk the demo path, make it believable |

## Flow

```
stage 1 → stage 2 → stage 3 → ┬─ stage 4a (no-code, Lovable)
                                └─ stage 4b → stage 5 ⇄ stage 6
```

Stages must run in order — each one reads the previous stage's artifact.

## Key file locations

- **Run folder**: `workshop/runs/<slug>/` — all artifacts land here (gitignored)
- **Brand file**: `apps/web/src/brand.js` — the one file stage 4b edits
- **Shared rules**: `.claude/skills/shared/HARNESS.md`
- **Worked example**: `workshop/examples/kora/` — a complete 7-stage run to reference

## Starter kit

```bash
npm install && npm run dev   # web :5173, api :3001
```

The app auto-seeds SQLite on first boot. `npm run seed` re-seeds. Port busy? Copy
`.env.example` → `.env` and set `API_PORT=3002`.

## Artifact saving

Every stage saves a branded HTML file to `workshop/runs/<slug>/`. See
`.claude/skills/shared/HARNESS.md` for the exact format and asset paths. Cursor
can write these files with the Edit/Write tools — the template and CSS are in
`.claude/skills/shared/`.
